<title>CANADA: United Grain Growers sets share issue.</title>
<headline>United Grain Growers sets share issue.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG, Manitoba 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Grain Growers Ltd, one of Canada's largest agricultural companies, said on Wednesday that it has entered an agreement to sell two million of its common shares at C$11 each to a syndicate of underwriters led by Canadian brokerage firm ScotiaMcLeod Inc.</p>
<p>UGG, which represents more than 100,000 farmers in Western Canada, said gross proceeds of the sale will be C$22 million.</p>
<p>The company also said it has granted the underwriters an option to purchase another 500,000 shares at a price of C$11 for a period of 48 hours.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto (416) 941-8100</p>
</text>
